          <h2 style="font-size: var(--fs-56); margin-bottom: var(--space-6);" data-en="Everything you need to know about a 10-yard dumpster." data-es="Todo lo que necesitas saber sobre un contenedor de 10 yardas.">Everything you need to know about a 10-yard dumpster.</h2>

          <h3 data-en="What is a 10-yard roll-off dumpster?" data-es="¿Qué es un contenedor roll-off de 10 yardas?">What is a 10-yard roll-off dumpster?</h3>
          <p data-html data-en="A 10-yard roll-off dumpster is the smallest container we deliver. It measures roughly <strong>12 feet long, 8 feet wide, and 3.5 feet tall</strong>, with an open top and a swing-out door on the back end so you can walk debris in instead of throwing it over the side. The &quot;10 yard&quot; name comes from cubic-yard volume: ten cubic yards of debris fits inside, which works out to about three full-size pickup truck loads." data-es="Un contenedor roll-off de 10 yardas es el contenedor más pequeño que entregamos. Mide aproximadamente <strong>12 pies de largo, 8 pies de ancho y 3.5 pies de alto</strong>, con la parte superior abierta y una puerta abatible en la parte trasera para que puedas meter los escombros caminando en lugar de lanzarlos por encima. El nombre &quot;10 yardas&quot; viene del volumen en yardas cúbicas: caben diez yardas cúbicas de escombros adentro, lo que equivale a unas tres cargas de camioneta de tamaño completo.">A 10-yard roll-off dumpster is the smallest container we deliver. It measures roughly <strong>12 feet long, 8 feet wide, and 3.5 feet tall</strong>, with an open top and a swing-out door on the back end so you can walk debris in instead of throwing it over the side. The "10 yard" name comes from cubic-yard volume: ten cubic yards of debris fits inside, which works out to about three full-size pickup truck loads.</p>
          <p data-html data-en="Roll-offs got the name because the dumpster <em>rolls off</em> the back of the delivery truck onto your driveway, then rolls back on when it's time to haul. There's no hopper, no compaction, no fixed dumpster on wheels — it's a steel container that gets set, filled, and pulled. Simple and predictable." data-es="Los roll-off reciben ese nombre porque el contenedor <em>rueda</em> desde la parte trasera del camión de entrega hasta tu entrada, y luego vuelve a subir cuando es hora de acarrearlo. No hay tolva, ni compactación, ni contenedor fijo con ruedas — es un contenedor de acero que se coloca, se llena y se retira. Simple y predecible.">Roll-offs got the name because the dumpster <em>rolls off</em> the back of the delivery truck onto your driveway, then rolls back on when it's time to haul. There's no hopper, no compaction, no fixed dumpster on wheels — it's a steel container that gets set, filled, and pulled. Simple and predictable.</p>

          <h3 data-en="Common 10-yard projects in the DMV" data-es="Proyectos comunes de 10 yardas en el DMV">Common 10-yard projects in the DMV</h3>
          <p data-en="The 10-yard is the right call when you've got a contained, one-room or single-zone cleanout. After more than 25 years of drops across Prince George's and Montgomery County, here's where we see it shine:" data-es="El de 10 yardas es la opción ideal cuando tienes una limpieza contenida, de una sola habitación o zona. Después de más de 25 años de entregas en los condados de Prince George's y Montgomery, aquí es donde más brilla:">The 10-yard is the right call when you've got a contained, one-room or single-zone cleanout. After more than 25 years of drops across Prince George's and Montgomery County, here's where we see it shine:</p>
          <ul>
            <li data-html data-en="<strong>Garage and basement cleanouts.</strong> Stored boxes, broken tools, holiday decor, empty paint cans, leftover lumber. A 10-yard handles a two-car garage's worth of accumulated stuff." data-es="<strong>Limpiezas de garaje y sótano.</strong> Cajas guardadas, herramientas rotas, decoración navideña, latas de pintura vacías, madera sobrante. Un contenedor de 10 yardas maneja lo acumulado en un garaje para dos autos."><strong>Garage and basement cleanouts.</strong> Stored boxes, broken tools, holiday decor, empty paint cans, leftover lumber. A 10-yard handles a two-car garage's worth of accumulated stuff.</li>
            <li data-html data-en="<strong>Single-bathroom remodels.</strong> Tear out a cast-iron tub, vanity, tile, drywall, and a toilet and you'll fit inside a 10-yard with room left over. Most full-bath demos clock in around 5–7 cubic yards." data-es="<strong>Remodelaciones de un solo baño.</strong> Quita una bañera de hierro fundido, mueble de lavabo, azulejo, panel de yeso y un inodoro y cabrás en uno de 10 yardas con espacio de sobra. La mayoría de las demoliciones de baño completo rondan las 5–7 yardas cúbicas."><strong>Single-bathroom remodels.</strong> Tear out a cast-iron tub, vanity, tile, drywall, and a toilet and you'll fit inside a 10-yard with room left over. Most full-bath demos clock in around 5–7 cubic yards.</li>
            <li data-html data-en="<strong>Yard waste and tree removal.</strong> Branches, brush, sod, mulch, leaves, a small uprooted tree. Yard waste is bulky but light, so volume hits before weight." data-es="<strong>Desechos del jardín y remoción de árboles.</strong> Ramas, maleza, césped, mantillo, hojas, un árbol pequeño desarraigado. Los desechos del jardín son voluminosos pero ligeros, así que el volumen se llena antes que el peso."><strong>Yard waste and tree removal.</strong> Branches, brush, sod, mulch, leaves, a small uprooted tree. Yard waste is bulky but light, so volume hits before weight.</li>
            <li data-html data-en="<strong>Estate downsizing or moving cleanouts.</strong> One bedroom or a small apartment's worth of furniture, mattresses, clothes, and household goods." data-es="<strong>Reducción de patrimonio o limpiezas por mudanza.</strong> Una habitación o el equivalente a un apartamento pequeño de muebles, colchones, ropa y artículos del hogar."><strong>Estate downsizing or moving cleanouts.</strong> One bedroom or a small apartment's worth of furniture, mattresses, clothes, and household goods.</li>
            <li data-html data-en="<strong>Small flooring or kitchen-tile rip-ups.</strong> If you're only pulling tile or hardwood from one room, a 10 is usually enough — unless the tile is thick or set on concrete board." data-es="<strong>Remoción de piso o azulejo de cocina pequeña.</strong> Si solo estás quitando azulejo o madera de una habitación, uno de 10 suele ser suficiente — a menos que el azulejo sea grueso o esté colocado sobre tablero de concreto."><strong>Small flooring or kitchen-tile rip-ups.</strong> If you're only pulling tile or hardwood from one room, a 10 is usually enough — unless the tile is thick or set on concrete board.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 data-en="How much weight can a 10-yard hold?" data-es="¿Cuánto peso aguanta uno de 10 yardas?">How much weight can a 10-yard hold?</h3>
          <p data-html data-en="Every 10-yard rental from JP Roll-Off includes a <strong>1-ton (2,000 lb) weight allowance</strong>. For perspective: a fully-loaded car-axle scale ticket on a typical garage cleanout runs 700–1,200 pounds. Most residential jobs stay comfortably inside the tonnage limit. If you go over, excess weight is billed at $105 per additional ton over the allowance." data-es="Cada renta de 10 yardas de JP Roll-Off incluye un <strong>límite de peso de 1 tonelada (2,000 lb)</strong>. Para que te hagas una idea: el ticket de báscula de una limpieza de garaje típica ronda las 700–1,200 libras. La mayoría de los trabajos residenciales se mantienen cómodamente dentro del límite de tonelaje. Si te excedes, el peso excedente se cobra a $105 por tonelada adicional sobre el límite.">Every 10-yard rental from JP Roll-Off includes a <strong>1-ton (2,000 lb) weight allowance</strong>. For perspective: a fully-loaded car-axle scale ticket on a typical garage cleanout runs 700–1,200 pounds. Most residential jobs stay comfortably inside the tonnage limit. If you go over, excess weight is billed at $105 per additional ton over the allowance.</p>
          <p data-html data-en="What fills the weight before the volume? Concrete, dirt, brick, roofing shingles, and plaster lath. Note that heavy aggregates like dirt, concrete, and asphalt only come in 10-, 15-, or 20-yard containers. If your job is mostly heavy materials, ask about our <a href=&quot;/services/15-yard-dumpster&quot;>15-yard heavy-debris quote</a> instead — you'll often pay less by going bigger on weight allowance." data-es="¿Qué llena el peso antes que el volumen? Concreto, tierra, ladrillo, tejas de techo y listones de yeso. Ten en cuenta que los agregados pesados como tierra, concreto y asfalto solo vienen en contenedores de 10, 15 o 20 yardas. Si tu trabajo es mayormente material pesado, pregunta por nuestra <a href=&quot;/services/15-yard-dumpster&quot;>cotización de escombros pesados de 15 yardas</a> — a menudo pagarás menos al elegir un tamaño mayor con más límite de peso.">What fills the weight before the volume? Concrete, dirt, brick, roofing shingles, and plaster lath. Note that heavy aggregates like dirt, concrete, and asphalt only come in 10-, 15-, or 20-yard containers. If your job is mostly heavy materials, ask about our <a href="/services/15-yard-dumpster">15-yard heavy-debris quote</a> instead — you'll often pay less by going bigger on weight allowance.</p>

          <h3 data-en="Where will the 10-yard fit on my property?" data-es="¿Dónde cabe el de 10 yardas en mi propiedad?">Where will the 10-yard fit on my property?</h3>
          <p data-en="This is the size people pick when driveway space is tight. A 10-yard fits in a single car spot — about the footprint of a midsize sedan — so you can keep the second half of the driveway clear for daily life. Standard placement options:" data-es="Este es el tamaño que la gente elige cuando el espacio en la entrada es limitado. Un contenedor de 10 yardas cabe en un solo lugar de auto — más o menos el espacio de un sedán mediano — para que puedas mantener la otra mitad de la entrada libre para el día a día. Opciones estándar de colocación:">This is the size people pick when driveway space is tight. A 10-yard fits in a single car spot — about the footprint of a midsize sedan — so you can keep the second half of the driveway clear for daily life. Standard placement options:</p>
          <ul>
            <li data-html data-en="<strong>Driveway, parallel to the house.</strong> Most common. We place 2×10 protective boards under the rails so there's no scarring on asphalt or concrete." data-es="<strong>Entrada, paralelo a la casa.</strong> Lo más común. Colocamos tablas protectoras de 2×10 bajo los rieles para que no haya marcas en el asfalto o el concreto."><strong>Driveway, parallel to the house.</strong> Most common. We place 2×10 protective boards under the rails so there's no scarring on asphalt or concrete.</li>
            <li data-html data-en="<strong>Driveway, perpendicular to the curb.</strong> Useful when you want to pull the door-end toward the work area for walk-in loading." data-es="<strong>Entrada, perpendicular a la acera.</strong> Útil cuando quieres acercar el lado de la puerta hacia el área de trabajo para cargar caminando."><strong>Driveway, perpendicular to the curb.</strong> Useful when you want to pull the door-end toward the work area for walk-in loading.</li>
            <li data-html data-en="<strong>Side yard or alleyway.</strong> If we can swing the truck in cleanly. Send a quick photo when you book and we'll spec it." data-es="<strong>Patio lateral o callejón.</strong> Si podemos maniobrar el camión sin problema. Envía una foto rápida al reservar y lo evaluamos."><strong>Side yard or alleyway.</strong> If we can swing the truck in cleanly. Send a quick photo when you book and we'll spec it.</li>
            <li data-html data-en="<strong>On the street (with permit).</strong> If your house has no driveway access, your jurisdiction can issue a temporary right-of-way permit. We'll walk you through it." data-es="<strong>En la calle (con permiso).</strong> Si tu casa no tiene acceso por la entrada, tu jurisdicción puede emitir un permiso temporal de derecho de paso. Te guiamos en el proceso."><strong>On the street (with permit).</strong> If your house has no driveway access, your jurisdiction can issue a temporary right-of-way permit. We'll walk you through it.</li>
          </ul>
